      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure that I get this. If we perform a setting to none immediately, and the AP mux gets out of sync with the other muxes, isn\u0027t that still bad?\n\nNote that mux task shouldn\u0027t block in clearing this entry from the queue, unless the virtual mux driver tells it to, and the virtual mux driver has its own logic for doing this: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/main/driver/usb_mux/virtual.c#68 If there should be a special case for `USB_PD_MUX_NONE`, it should probably be in that driver.\n\nIf the concern here is instead that this change will wait on a queue full of already-blocked HPD updates that need acks, and it\u0027s considered permissible to apply the mux changes out of order, then the appropriate change might be to modify the Hard Reset logic to directly clear the mux queue and then enqueue the final change to none as normal.",
      "revId": "ca91e5b3fdef60fe95e400538614e901102094a7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
